  "details": "When scaling down using avatar scaling, the way stereo seperation and positional audio is calculated does not adjust to compensate for scale.\n\nThe result of this is that when there are a lot of users standing in a circle close together with small scale, the audio processing makes it sound like everyone is whispering into each others ear with extreme stereo separation of channels.\n\nMy guess is that while the camera IPD scales down with the avatar the \"ear to ear\" distance does not get adjusted properly.",
